## Supervisor Review Summary — exp042 Residual Amp Diffusion

### Experiment Reviewed
**exp042**: Residual Amp Diffusion — train diffusion on `(gt_amp - AmpPredictor_mean)` instead of full amp. 300 epochs, evaluated at η=0.3.

### Key Metrics
| Metric | exp039 (best deterministic) | exp042 (residual diffusion) | Delta |
|--------|---------------------------|----------------------------|-------|
| **Amp Corr** | **0.807** | **0.744** | **-0.063 ❌** |
| Amp RMSE(log) | 0.582 | 0.699 | +0.117 |
| f0 RPA | 93.73% | 94.31% | +0.58% |
| amp_diversity | ~0 | 0.004 | +0.004 ✅ |

### Critical Finding
**Quality floor mechanism FAILED.** Expected Amp Corr ≥ 0.80 (AmpPredictor should guarantee a floor), but got 0.744. Root cause: the diffusion model outputs non-trivial residuals that correlate with training data but are essentially noise on test data, corrupting the AmpPredictor's good predictions.

### Code Review
✅ **No bugs found.** Normalization stats match exactly between exp039 and exp042. The residual computation and inference pipeline are mathematically correct. The issue is purely that the learned residual model doesn't generalize.

